!! NAT/PAT - BONUS :)



!!! https://www.firewall.cx/cisco-technical-knowledgebase/cisco-routers/260-cisco-router-nat-overload.html
access-list 100 remark == [Control NAT Service]==
access-list 100 permit ip 192.168.0.0 0.0.0.255 any

ip nat inside source list 100 interface FastEthernet0/0 overload


interface FastEthernet0/0
description ip address dhcp - To ISP1 via FastEthernet0/0 DHCP - NS
ip address dhcp
ip nat outside
shutdown
no shutdown


interface FastEthernet1/0
description ip address 192.168.0.1 255.255.255.0 - To local network - NS
ip address 192.168.0.1 255.255.255.0
ip nat inside
shutdown
no shutdown
